    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's what I changed to make owner deletion a soft-delete:\n\n**Domain model** \u2014 `Owner.java`: added a `deleted` boolean field (default `false`, mapped to a new `deleted` column) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`.\n\n**Delete behaviour** \u2014 `DeleteOwner.java`: instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s, so the row is retained and the endpoint still returns 2xx.\n\n**Create checks** \u2014 `CheckIdentityUnique.java`: the loop over existing owners now skips any owner flagged `deleted`, so both the exact-identity and household duplicate rules ignore soft-deleted owners \u2014 a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was deleted.\n\n**Response contract** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically. GET now returns `deleted: false` for a fresh owner and `true` after deletion.\n\n**Schema/data** \u2014 added the `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and appended the value to the positional seed inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the only one using positional inserts).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains`, `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck`) and the full suite pass.",
